WEBVTT

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:04.930
This is your reporter, Mirai Kamiki.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.390
In the Gunpla Battle Japanese
Under-19 Championship,

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.480
both matches of the semifinals...

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:15.850
...have recently been completed.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.110
And the winners of those battles are...

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:22.490
The champions for six years
running, Gunpla Academy,

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.860
representing Shizuoka,
team Celestial Sphere.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:28.780
And some first-timers
making amazing progress,

00:00:28.780 --> 00:00:31.790
Seiho Academy Middle School,
representing West Tokyo,

00:00:31.910 --> 00:00:33.460
team Try Fighters!

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.420
<i>The final round will be in two days.</i>

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.800
<i>That's when these two teams
will face each other...</i>

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:42.260
Need a hand, Big Brother?

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.380
No, I can do it myself.

00:00:44.470 --> 00:00:45.180
But...

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.430
Leave him be.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:51.140
He thinks he has to
pull this off by himself,

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:55.730
or the open tournament will
be merely a dream for him.

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.730
Don't try to read my mind.

00:00:58.980 --> 00:01:02.360
Shia, would you tune
The End for me?

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:07.820
I want to increase the fangs'
reaction speed by at least 2 percent.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:11.330
Okay. I got it.

00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.830
This year's tournament is good.

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.630
It's seriously awesome.

00:01:24.170 --> 00:01:29.180
To think, we have to fix these
before the final round.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:32.350
I'm sorry. If I'd done better...

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:33.890
We'll fix them for sure!

00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.140
Sekai, back me up.

00:01:36.230 --> 00:01:37.230
Sure thing.

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:38.900
I'll do anything I can.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:40.770
Me, too!

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:41.900
Thanks, guys!

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.990
Let's combine our strength
and fix our Gunpla!

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:47.200
Yeah!
Yeah!

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:11.050
<i>Our wings couldn't wait for the wind, so we set out</i>

00:02:11.050 --> 00:02:16.560
<i>We were bathed in the light of the frozen sun</i>

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:19.310
<i>Oh Oh Oh Oh Oh there are no limits</i>

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:22.060
<i>Oh Oh Oh Oh Oh just let it go</i>

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:27.610
<i>Oh Oh Oh Oh Oh loneliness won't break us</i>

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:32.160
<i>At the end of the dream we'll never give up,</i>

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.790
<i>Will there be a future that can never end?</i>

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:40.370
<i>Believe in what only you can do</i>

00:02:40.370 --> 00:02:43.090
<i>If I could seize one thing,</i>

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:45.800
<i>I'd choose it without hesitation</i>

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:51.090
<i>Follow your instincts, just hold on to our bond</i>

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:57.640
Up to the endless sky, now! Fly away

00:03:15.580 --> 00:03:19.000
<i>GUNDAM BUILD FIGHTERS TRY</i>

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:22.960
Episode 23
Build Fighter

00:03:24.130 --> 00:03:27.880
Let's rest our hands a minute
and start our briefing.

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:31.720
Wouldn't it be better
to talk after we've seen...

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.640
...the Gunpla Academy's battle
on the tournament TV show?

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:37.060
Oh, there's no need for that.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:41.140
We have the match records
and some very detailed data.

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.060
They're on this memory chip.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.520
Where did you get that?

00:03:46.270 --> 00:03:51.030
Shiki from Niigata's Toritsu
Academy sent it to me by e-mail.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.990
Toritsu Academy?

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.990
Those guys with the dragon?

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.950
There was a message with it, too.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:01.960
"You'd better put up a decent fight."

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:05.630
"Otherwise we'll be rated lower
because we lost to you."

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:07.170
So it says.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.510
Such a backhanded compliment...

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:11.720
But we should thank them.

00:04:12.760 --> 00:04:14.930
Mr. Ral, please show us the video.

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.300
Of course.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:20.390
First is Wilfrid Kijima's
Transient Gundam.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.700
It pierced the floating island...

00:04:38.370 --> 00:04:40.870
Its power is different from
what we saw at training camp.

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:45.040
He was holding back
until his fight with Sekai.

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.670
And he has another trump card.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.720
A Burst System?!

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:02.020
Just like the Try Burning...

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:03.310
That's right.

00:05:03.390 --> 00:05:05.390
It's a particle emission system.

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:09.730
Next is Saga Adou's Gundam The End.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:13.740
You've already fought it,
so no need for details.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:16.910
But it had some hidden functions.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:19.240
It's got something in its belly!

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:22.870
It has such gimmicks? Unbelievable.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.000
Mr. Ral.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:26.290
What about the video of
Miss Shia Kijima's G-Portent?

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.380
It's up next.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:31.710
I'm most concerned
about a certain scene.

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:34.460
It was hit?!

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:37.260
Mr. Ral, what's your concern?

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.220
Look at the screen.

00:05:43.350 --> 00:05:44.930
Something came out.

00:05:46.890 --> 00:05:49.440
Those little things
are fixing the Gunpla!

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:51.770
Are those Karel
maintenance machines?

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.280
That can't be.

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.110
There's no function that fixes
Gunpla in the battle system.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:06:00.490
It's not the battle system.
They're actually fixing it.

00:06:00.950 --> 00:06:02.030
What?

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:04.490
For making repairs,
the Karels must be...

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:08.460
...carrying stuff like instant glue
and quick-drying putty.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:13.130
But a 1/144 Karel would be...

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:15.260
...about this small.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:18.380
Even I could make one.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:21.140
What's astonishing is...

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:27.060
...that she was able to control
five tiny repair machines all at once...

00:06:27.350 --> 00:06:29.650
...and fix the damaged
parts during combat.

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:32.610
That's how amazing
her skills as a builder are.

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:37.820
So they can fix the Gunpla
whenever it gets hurt.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.660
Then we shouldn't give
them time to fix it.

00:06:42.740 --> 00:06:47.410
But if the final battlefield is a
complex one with places to hide,

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:52.380
this repair function will be
a huge advantage for them.

00:06:53.130 --> 00:06:56.510
The longer the battle,
the bigger our disadvantage.

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:59.340
Kijima is an all-rounder.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:02.970
Adou has overwhelming
offensive strength.

00:07:03.350 --> 00:07:06.520
And Shia Kijima has
a repair function.

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.730
It's a perfect lineup.

00:07:12.020 --> 00:07:13.980
So this is the six-time champion...

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:16.980
This is the Gunpla
Academy's true strength.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.700
Thank you.

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:34.080
Most people only see you fighting
brilliantly in the battlefield.

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:38.340
They'd never imagine
how much effort you put into it.

00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.010
It's no effort.

00:07:41.170 --> 00:07:43.430
I love Gunpla, so I'm just building one.

00:07:45.050 --> 00:07:49.350
I didn't make you team leader
just because of your ability.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:53.850
I chose you for your
sincere attitude toward Gunpla.

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:56.310
You really remind me of...

00:07:57.230 --> 00:07:59.230
...the third Meijin Kawaguchi.

00:07:59.440 --> 00:08:01.950
No, of Tatsuya Yuuki.

00:08:03.700 --> 00:08:06.660
So I've succeeded in
becoming a Gunpla freak?

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:09.160
That pure feeling you have...

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:11.750
Make sure you never forget it.

00:08:11.910 --> 00:08:13.460
Yes, Uncle.

00:08:14.500 --> 00:08:16.290
I mean, Coach.

00:08:16.710 --> 00:08:18.000
It's fine.

00:08:18.670 --> 00:08:21.340
I said those words as your uncle.

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:35.440
<i>Just restoring it isn't enough...</i>

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.770
...to <i>close the gap between us
and the Gunpla Academy,</i>

00:08:39.070 --> 00:08:42.240
<i>but there's no time for tuning.</i>

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:46.950
Yuuma, aren't you fixing it?

00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:51.160
<i>There's no other option. I'll do it!</i>

00:08:52.000 --> 00:08:54.330
Hey, what are you doing, Yuuma?

00:08:58.290 --> 00:09:00.300
Wh-Where are you going, Yuuma?

00:09:00.500 --> 00:09:02.380
What are you doing with the Gunpla?!

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.510
Miss Fumina, I brought you
paint and plastic boards.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.810
Thank you, Gyanko!

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:12.970
I'm sorry to ask you for this.

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:15.270
That's okay, but...

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:18.270
Who can it be?

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.940
I'll answer, so keep working.

00:09:21.480 --> 00:09:22.730
Thanks.

00:09:23.030 --> 00:09:24.490
Wh-What are you...?

00:09:25.990 --> 00:09:27.030
You?

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:32.870
Hoshino, I'm borrowing the Winning.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:34.120
What?

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:35.330
Excuse me.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:38.000
Wait...

00:09:38.250 --> 00:09:39.750
Wait a minute, Yuu!

00:09:42.090 --> 00:09:44.050
What are you doing, Yuuma?

00:09:46.220 --> 00:09:47.220
Sekai.

00:09:47.800 --> 00:09:48.760
Hoshino.

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:50.180
What happened?

00:09:50.260 --> 00:09:54.020
He said he had to work alone
on something important...

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:56.020
...and suddenly kicked me out.

00:09:57.230 --> 00:09:59.520
So what's Yuu up to?

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:02.190
I haven't got a clue...

00:10:05.190 --> 00:10:06.530
<i>Don't hesitate.</i>

00:10:06.820 --> 00:10:08.780
<i>If you have enough time to worry,</i>

00:10:09.160 --> 00:10:11.870
<i>then just move! Move forward...!</i>

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:15.790
Hello? Hoshino?

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:17.370
Yeah.

00:10:18.040 --> 00:10:19.830
I'm in my sister's room.

00:10:20.040 --> 00:10:23.960
Yuuma's staying up all night.
Bring him some food, okay?

00:10:24.130 --> 00:10:25.260
Gotcha.

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:27.800
Sorry, sis.

00:10:28.300 --> 00:10:30.680
Thanks for letting me crash here.

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:34.760
ls it okay for Kousaka
to push himself so hard?

00:10:35.390 --> 00:10:37.230
Hoshino will go and see him.

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:39.770
I'm going out now.

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:45.400
This should be enough.

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:51.910
J-Jun...

00:10:54.950 --> 00:10:57.120
What brings you here?

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.370
Oh, you know...

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:04.340
Just a little unfinished business.

00:11:05.460 --> 00:11:07.340
Yuuma's working alone?

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:10.430
<i>I'm worried. So I'll go check on him.</i>

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:13.800
I have Sekai's key.

00:11:14.140 --> 00:11:15.180
<i>Okay.</i>

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:16.850
Thanks.

00:11:21.190 --> 00:11:22.600
Reinforcements, eh?

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:27.320
I'm coming in.

00:11:31.950 --> 00:11:33.110
What?

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:34.320
Hey, Yuuma!

00:11:35.870 --> 00:11:37.240
Minato Sakai.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.290
What are you...?

00:11:43.170 --> 00:11:44.290
I see.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:48.050
That's some serious remodeling
before the final round.

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:50.340
You're in the way. Get out.

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:53.930
Give me the parts.

00:11:54.720 --> 00:11:57.470
You won't make it in time
if you do it alone.

00:12:01.430 --> 00:12:02.730
J-Jun!

00:12:03.060 --> 00:12:04.650
What are you doing?!

00:12:05.190 --> 00:12:07.270
Like I said, we've got
unfinished business.

00:12:08.530 --> 00:12:09.690
Are you serious?

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:10.990
You bet.

00:12:17.370 --> 00:12:18.540
<i>Four chopping hands?!</i>

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:24.870
Sekai.

00:12:27.090 --> 00:12:28.130
Remember that technique.

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:29.050
Remember that technique.

00:12:29.050 --> 00:12:29.500
Remember that technique.

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:41.890
Inspiring a younger pupil
with your technique?

00:12:41.890 --> 00:12:42.350
Inspiring a younger pupil
with your technique?

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.310
So you can be nice.

00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:50.980
Sekai is an amateur at Gunpla.

00:12:51.570 --> 00:12:52.740
I'm evening things up.

00:12:52.740 --> 00:12:53.570
I'm evening things up.

00:12:56.280 --> 00:12:57.030
Hey.

00:12:58.070 --> 00:12:59.700
Aren't you getting in?

00:12:59.700 --> 00:13:00.990
Of course not.

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:02.080
Get in.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:02.910
I said no.
Get in.

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.370
It's okay, come on.

00:13:04.370 --> 00:13:05.870
Absolutely never.

00:13:05.870 --> 00:13:07.830
There's nothing to worry about.

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:08.790
No way.

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:21.470
What is this?

00:13:21.930 --> 00:13:24.020
We're fully remodeling
all the machines.

00:13:24.390 --> 00:13:25.940
Why are you helping?

00:13:26.440 --> 00:13:30.150
Shouldn't you be building
a new piece for the Meijin Cup?

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:31.730
That's nonsense.

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:34.240
If I had more building time,

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:36.820
Mr. Crafty Glasses
would make excuses.

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:38.820
What did you call me?!

00:13:39.030 --> 00:13:41.120
I never said it was you.

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:47.120
Thanks.

00:13:49.750 --> 00:13:51.130
Aren't I a good guy?

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:53.050
You should be grateful.

00:13:53.050 --> 00:13:55.880
If you hadn't just said that...

00:13:55.880 --> 00:13:58.130
...you would've seemed
like a really great guy.

00:13:58.550 --> 00:14:00.260
I'm not into that.

00:14:00.470 --> 00:14:01.640
I'm not either!

00:14:01.640 --> 00:14:02.390
I said I'm not!

00:14:02.390 --> 00:14:03.310
That's what I said!

00:14:03.310 --> 00:14:03.560
I said, I'm not!

00:14:03.560 --> 00:14:04.350
I said, I'm not!
Even though they're arguing,

00:14:04.350 --> 00:14:05.060
That's what I said!
Even though they're arguing,

00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:05.480
I said, I'm not!
Even though they're arguing,

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:05.980
That's what I said!
Even though they're arguing,

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:06.390
I said, I'm not!
Even though they're arguing,

00:14:06.390 --> 00:14:06.980
That's what I said!
they're working with amazing speed.

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:07.480
I said, I'm not!
they're working with amazing speed.

00:14:07.480 --> 00:14:07.810
That's what I said!
they're working with amazing speed.

00:14:07.810 --> 00:14:08.520
I said, I'm not!
they're working with amazing speed.

00:14:08.520 --> 00:14:08.980
I'm telling you, I'm not!
they're working with amazing speed.

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:09.480
I'm telling you, I'm not!

00:14:09.480 --> 00:14:09.980
I'm telling you, I'm not!
I know!!

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:20.740
You're taking a nap out here?

00:14:24.830 --> 00:14:26.540
You must be joking.

00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.250
Ouch...

00:14:28.580 --> 00:14:30.880
Jun was serious.

00:14:31.790 --> 00:14:34.960
But that technique wasn't
from the Jigen Haoh School.

00:14:35.300 --> 00:14:36.420
Huh?

00:14:36.670 --> 00:14:37.670
Nothing.

00:14:39.130 --> 00:14:41.300
Can the damaged
Gunpla be fixed?

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:42.680
Yeah.

00:14:43.970 --> 00:14:47.520
My brother's Gunpla was
also broken in the semifinals.

00:14:48.180 --> 00:14:50.440
I tried to help him fix it,

00:14:50.850 --> 00:14:53.190
but he said he'd do it alone.

00:14:55.020 --> 00:14:57.820
I envy Wilfrid Kijima.

00:14:58.530 --> 00:14:59.360
Why?

00:15:00.820 --> 00:15:05.410
I don't have the skill
to fix such complex Gunpla,

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:09.290
so I'm always causing trouble
for Yuuma and Hoshino.

00:15:10.000 --> 00:15:13.460
What's wrong with that?
You're a great fighter.

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:17.710
I'll build you a good Gunpla, and...

00:15:18.880 --> 00:15:20.340
That won't work.

00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:21.930
What?

00:15:23.970 --> 00:15:27.100
Up until three months ago,

00:15:27.350 --> 00:15:30.190
I didn't know anything
about Gunpla or Gunpla Battle.

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:36.820
Hoshino invited me
to try moving Gunpla,

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:41.280
and I found I could use my
Jigen Haoh School of Kenpo in battle.

00:15:43.740 --> 00:15:45.330
I enjoyed it so much.

00:15:45.870 --> 00:15:49.410
We won the regional qualifiers,
and made it to the nationals.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:53.920
I knew that I'd get to fight
even stronger opponents...

00:15:54.080 --> 00:15:56.130
I was so excited.

00:15:58.800 --> 00:16:00.220
I still feel that way.

00:16:02.760 --> 00:16:06.430
But I don't truly understand Gunpla.

00:16:09.430 --> 00:16:11.640
I don't know how they feel...

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:15.860
Yuuma, Hoshino, and the other
Gunpla lovers I've fought.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.780
I can't become their equal...

00:16:21.610 --> 00:16:23.780
...until I learn more about Gunpla,

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:27.410
and can handle things myself.

00:16:30.160 --> 00:16:31.330
I see.

00:16:31.790 --> 00:16:33.830
My big brother must feel the same.

00:16:36.210 --> 00:16:39.750
Boy, I let out what's been
weighing on my mind.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:41.460
I feel refreshed.

00:16:42.130 --> 00:16:45.180
I'll go back to the others
and help fix our Gunpla.

00:16:46.300 --> 00:16:48.140
Let's meet at tomorrow's finals.

00:16:49.060 --> 00:16:49.760
Yes.

00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:53.310
At the finals...

00:16:53.480 --> 00:16:54.480
See ya!

00:16:58.980 --> 00:17:00.150
Build fighter.

00:17:05.150 --> 00:17:06.780
<i>I'm a beginner.</i>

00:17:07.200 --> 00:17:09.990
<i>There's so much to learn
and so much I lack.</i>

00:17:12.080 --> 00:17:13.450
<i>I want to be...</i>

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:19.290
<i>...worthy of the Try Burning
that Mr. Sei lori entrusted to me.</i>

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.340
<i>When I reach that height...</i>

00:17:26.590 --> 00:17:29.680
<i>...then I can call myself,
loud and proud,</i>

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:35.730
<i>a Gundam build fighter.</i>

00:17:45.240 --> 00:17:46.360
Over here!

00:17:46.360 --> 00:17:47.490
Sorry I'm late.

00:17:48.160 --> 00:17:50.280
I was picking my brother up.

00:17:50.370 --> 00:17:52.450
I worked hard on my rehab,

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:54.870
so the doctor let me go out.

00:17:55.370 --> 00:17:57.040
Wow, you did good.

00:18:01.040 --> 00:18:02.130
Big brother.

00:18:02.210 --> 00:18:03.420
What, Mamoru?

00:18:03.800 --> 00:18:05.720
Which one's your girlfriend?

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:08.340
Wh-What do you mean?

00:18:08.800 --> 00:18:10.010
What a precocious child.

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:11.350
How awkward.

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:17.190
I have nothing more to say.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.400
Enjoy the Gunpla Battle.

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:21.440
Right.
Yes.

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:23.730
I'll win for sure.

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:26.650
What's wrong, Shia?

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:28.700
You're all fired up.

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:32.080
I want to be one, too...

00:18:32.580 --> 00:18:34.700
I will defeat him,

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:37.250
and become a true build fighter.

00:18:41.750 --> 00:18:44.340
I'm looking forward
to the final round.

00:18:44.750 --> 00:18:49.380
Ms. Lady, if we win,
will you fight me again?

00:18:49.630 --> 00:18:51.050
Of course.

00:18:51.140 --> 00:18:53.300
If you win, I'll be
the one asking you.

00:18:54.760 --> 00:18:57.100
I'll definitely try my hardest
to surpass you!

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:03.060
What a saucy girl.

00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:06.860
But... I like it.

00:19:09.780 --> 00:19:13.240
Thank you all for waiting.

00:19:14.620 --> 00:19:18.200
<i>We now begin the 13th Gunpla Battle...</i>

00:19:18.660 --> 00:19:22.130
<i>...Japanese Under-19 Championship...</i>

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:23.630
<i>...final round!</i>

00:19:24.460 --> 00:19:29.380
<i>Representing Shizuoka, Gunpla Academy,
team Celestial Sphere versus...</i>

00:19:29.670 --> 00:19:33.140
<i>...representing West Tokyo,
Seiho Academy Middle School,</i>

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:36.060
<i>team Try Fighters.
This is their battle!</i>

00:19:38.730 --> 00:19:41.640
<i>Sei, the final match
is about to start.</i>

00:19:45.270 --> 00:19:47.820
Sekai, Yuu.

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:50.990
Thanks for joining my team.

00:19:52.320 --> 00:19:54.320
It's I who should be thankful.

00:19:55.120 --> 00:19:57.330
You've always been
looking out for me.

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:00.160
That's how I found
my way back to battle.

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:02.870
I'm grateful, too.

00:20:03.120 --> 00:20:05.080
If I hadn't met you...

00:20:05.290 --> 00:20:08.920
...l might have never
played Gunpla Battle.

00:20:10.260 --> 00:20:12.010
A lot's happened with us.

00:20:13.010 --> 00:20:15.140
I recognized my own weakness.

00:20:15.850 --> 00:20:18.100
I met so many rivals.

00:20:18.260 --> 00:20:21.480
I came to love Gunpla even more.

00:20:22.350 --> 00:20:25.650
This final round is our conclusion.

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:26.980
Let's give it our all...

00:20:27.110 --> 00:20:29.320
...and fight 'til the end with a smile!

00:20:30.190 --> 00:20:31.860
Team Try Fighters...

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:34.070
Go...
Go...

00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:35.450
"fight!
"fight!

00:20:36.200 --> 00:20:38.450
Gunpla Academy Seiho Academy

00:20:39.370 --> 00:20:43.040
<i>Gunpla Battle, combat mode, startup.</i>

00:20:43.710 --> 00:20:46.540
<i>Model damage level, set to A.</i>

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:50.000
Please set your GP Base.

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:57.050
<i>Beginning Plavsky particle dispersal.</i>

00:20:58.810 --> 00:21:01.180
<i>Field 1, Space.</i>

00:21:02.180 --> 00:21:03.940
Please set your Gunpla.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:12.150
<i>Battle start.</i>

00:21:13.320 --> 00:21:15.910
Fumina Hoshino, Star Winning Gundam.

00:21:16.320 --> 00:21:19.830
Yuuma Kousaka,
Lightning Gundam Full Burnern.

00:21:20.490 --> 00:21:23.250
Sekai Kamiki, Try Burning Gundam.

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:26.420
Saga Adou, Gundam The End.

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.880
Shia Kijima, G-Portent.

00:21:29.170 --> 00:21:31.840
Wilfrid Kijima, Transient Gundam.

00:21:32.670 --> 00:21:34.840
Team Celestial Sphere, fly away!

00:21:35.680 --> 00:21:36.680
Let's go hunting!

00:21:36.880 --> 00:21:37.680
Here I go!

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:40.890
Team Try Fighters, here we go!

00:21:40.970 --> 00:21:41.930
Launch!

00:21:41.930 --> 00:21:42.720
Go!

00:21:47.190 --> 00:21:50.860
There's so much I still lack.

00:21:51.820 --> 00:21:54.570
But I'll fight them
with everything I have.

00:21:54.990 --> 00:21:57.910
Let's go, Try Burning!

00:22:11.670 --> 00:22:14.760
<i>There's a tomorrow I want to touch</i>

00:22:14.760 --> 00:22:18.130
<i>I want to prove it for myself</i>

00:22:18.130 --> 00:22:22.930
<i>Love, hate, which is it?</i>

00:22:23.680 --> 00:22:26.770
<i>Perhaps the challenge is in the journey</i>

00:22:26.770 --> 00:22:29.850
<i>Wandering the unknown path...</i>

00:22:29.850 --> 00:22:36.610
<i>...toward abundant happiness</i>

00:22:38.360 --> 00:22:41.320
<i>I was afraid to run</i>

00:22:41.320 --> 00:22:44.740
<i>But now that I've started, I can't stop</i>

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:47.540
<i>I must've been waiting for the go sign</i>

00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:51.380
<i>With this passion in my impatient heart,</i>

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:56.050
<i>I want to search for something</i>

00:22:56.050 --> 00:23:00.800
<i>Let's meet over and over again (with you)</i>

00:23:00.800 --> 00:23:03.100
<i>On this journey, can you show me...</i>

00:23:03.100 --> 00:23:08.140
...a <i>different truth? (let me see)</i>

00:23:08.140 --> 00:23:15.070
<i>The power to find new things (with me)</i>

00:23:15.070 --> 00:23:18.650
<i>Never forget it</i>

00:23:18.650 --> 00:23:20.950
<i>Bring the real you to meet the real me</i>

00:23:20.950 --> 00:23:21.490
<i>(Today)
Bring the real you to meet the real me</i>

00:23:21.490 --> 00:23:23.120
<i>(Today)
As we travel, you smile at me</i>

00:23:23.120 --> 00:23:23.990
<i>(I'll be there...)
As we travel, you smile at me</i>

00:23:23.990 --> 00:23:26.990
<i>(I'll be there...)
I love it, I love it, this journey without a compass</i>

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:29.370
<i>(Alive!)
I love it, I love it, this journey without a compass</i>

00:23:29.370 --> 00:23:30.330
<i>(Alive!)</i>

00:23:30.370 --> 00:23:36.210
Team Try Fighters!

00:23:43.640 --> 00:23:44.970
Adou...

00:23:46.970 --> 00:23:49.270
So, you're participating after all.

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:52.560
You can't keep fighting.

00:23:53.560 --> 00:23:55.230
Your right wrist is...

00:23:55.770 --> 00:23:57.480
...already past its limit.

00:24:00.740 --> 00:24:02.570
There's nothing more to say.

00:24:02.740 --> 00:24:05.160
Let's give it our all and win!

00:24:05.570 --> 00:24:06.280
Next episode, "Final Burst".

00:24:06.280 --> 00:24:07.450
Final Burst
Next episode, "Final Burst".

00:24:07.450 --> 00:24:09.540
Final Burst
Rage on, Gunpla!

00:24:09.540 --> 00:24:09.910
Final Burst
